@startuml API Endpoints Overview

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFACD

package "Products API" #LightBlue {
  [ProductController] as ProductCtrl
  
  note right of ProductCtrl
    **Base Path**: /products
    
    **GET /products?excludeTagIds=1,2,3**
    • Purpose: Get products with tag exclusion filter
    • Query Param: excludeTagIds (comma-separated tag IDs)
    • Logic: Returns products that do NOT have any of the specified tags
    • Response: ProductResponse[] with tags included
    • Use Case: Filter menu for allergies/dietary restrictions
    
    **GET /products/category/{categoryId}**
    • Purpose: Get products by category
    • Response: ProductResponse[] with tags included
    • Use Case: Display products in a specific category
    
    **POST /products**
    • Purpose: Create new product
    • Body: ProductRequest
    • Response: ProductResponse with tags (empty initially)
    
    **PUT /products/{id}**
    • Purpose: Update existing product
    • Body: ProductRequest
    • Response: ProductResponse with tags
    
    **DELETE /products/{id}**
    • Purpose: Delete product
    • Effect: Cascades to product_tag relationships
  end note
}

package "Product Tags API" #LightGreen {
  [ProductTagController] as ProductTagCtrl
  
  note right of ProductTagCtrl
    **Base Path**: /product-tags
    
    **GET /product-tags/product/{productId}/tags**
    • Purpose: Get all tags for a specific product
    • Response: TagResponse[]
    • Use Case: Display tags on product card
    
    **POST /product-tags/product/{productId}/tag/{tagId}**
    • Purpose: Assign a tag to a product
    • Creates: product_tag relationship
    • Idempotent: No error if relationship exists
    
    **DELETE /product-tags/product/{productId}/tag/{tagId}**
    • Purpose: Remove tag from product
    • Deletes: product_tag relationship
    • Safe: No error if relationship doesn't exist
  end note
}

package "Tags API" #LightYellow {
  [TagController] as TagCtrl
  
  note right of TagCtrl
    **Base Path**: /tags
    
    **GET /tags**
    • Purpose: Get all available tags
    • Response: TagResponse[]
    • Use Case: Populate tag filter bar
    
    **GET /tags/{id}**
    • Purpose: Get single tag by ID
    • Response: TagResponse
    
    **POST /tags**
    • Purpose: Create new tag
    • Body: TagRequest (name, svgIcon)
    • Response: TagResponse
    
    **PUT /tags/{id}**
    • Purpose: Update tag
    • Body: TagRequest
    • Response: TagResponse
    
    **DELETE /tags/{id}**
    • Purpose: Delete tag
    • Effect: Cascades to product_tag relationships
  end note
}

' Show relationships and data flow
ProductCtrl ..> ProductTagCtrl : "manages relationships\nvia separate controller"
ProductCtrl ..> TagCtrl : "fetches tag data\nfor product enrichment"

note bottom of ProductCtrl
  **Key Feature: Tag Exclusion Filtering**
  
  Example Request:
  GET /products?excludeTagIds=1,2,3
  
  What Happens:
  1. Parse tag IDs: [1, 2, 3]
  2. Query database: Find products WITHOUT these tags
  3. SQL: WHERE product_id NOT IN (
       SELECT product_id FROM product_tag
       WHERE tag_id IN (1, 2, 3)
     )
  4. Enrich each product with its tags
  5. Return filtered products with tags included
  
  Result: User sees only products safe for their dietary needs
end note

note bottom of ProductTagCtrl
  **Separation of Concerns**
  
  Product-tag relationships are managed
  separately from product CRUD operations.
  This provides:
  • Better code organization
  • Clearer Swagger documentation
  • Easier maintenance
end note

note bottom
  **Swagger Documentation**
  All endpoints documented with:
  • @Operation: Summary and description
  • @Parameter: Path/query param details
  • @Tag: Groups endpoints in Swagger UI
  
  Access: http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui
  
  **Response Format**
  All product endpoints include tags array:
  {
    "id": 1,
    "name": "Pizza",
    "tags": [
      {"id": 1, "name": "Gluten"},
      {"id": 2, "name": "Dairy"}
    ]
  }
end note

@enduml

